# Build and packaging output.
/build/
/dist/
/bin/
*.egg-info/

# Byte-code and caches.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Tool virtualenvs and caches.  `make tools` creates .venv-tools; `make binary`
# creates .venv-build.  Neither is ever committed: the Makefile pins the tool
# versions and can rebuild both from scratch.
# A glob rather than a list: the Makefile creates .venv-tools, .venv-build and
# a throwaway .venv-test, and the next target to need an isolated environment
# should not also need a .gitignore edit.
/.venv*/
/venv/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# Internal documentation: kept on the developer's machine, never published.
# CLAUDE.md and .claude/ are written for people working *on* leafdump, and this
# repository is the public one. `make docs-check` fails if either is ever
# staged, because .gitignore alone does not stop `git add -f` and does nothing
# about a path that is already tracked.
#
# The whole of .claude/ rather than named files inside it: settings.local.json
# accumulates absolute paths to unrelated checkouts on this disk, and the next
# thing the tool writes there should not need a .gitignore edit to stay private.
/CLAUDE.md
/.claude/

# The same rule for everyone else's assistant. Not every contributor uses the
# same tool, and each invents its own dotfile; these are ignored so they never
# even show up as untracked noise. `make docs-check` is the backstop that
# actually enforces it -- ignoring a path does nothing once it is tracked.
#
# Several of these are worse than private notes. .mcp.json holds server
# definitions whose env blocks carry API tokens, .continue/config.json and
# .aider.conf.yml can hold model keys, and .aider.chat.history.md is a verbatim
# transcript of whatever was discussed.
/AGENTS.md
/GEMINI.md
/.codex/
/.mcp.json
/.cursorrules
/.cursor/
/.gemini/
/.windsurfrules
/.windsurf/
/.clinerules
/.roo/
/.roorules
/.roomodes
/.continue/
/.continuerc.json
/.aider*
/.amazonq/
/.junie/
/.augment/
/.augment-guidelines
/.kilocode/
/.openhands/
/.sourcegraph/
/.ai/
/.github/copilot-instructions.md
/.github/instructions/
/.github/prompts/

# Written by `make hooks`, and machine-specific: it holds an absolute path to
# the lefthook binary in this clone.
/.lefthook-rc.sh

# Nuitka scratch, if a build is ever pointed somewhere other than build/.
*.build/
*.dist/
*.onefile-build/

# Personal data, and everything build_events.py renders from it.  The exports
# are a medical journal; they stay on the machine that made them, and git
# history is the wrong place to learn that a file was private.
# Anchored to the root so the contrib/ fixtures -- which are test data and are
# committed -- keep matching their own names.
/ggg*.json
/ggg*.leafdump
/fff*.jcal
/events.md
/events.pdf
